{
  "_about": "The names Hasura v2 generates for the same tables under hasura-default and graphql-default (REQ-194, amended 2026-11-20). No Hasura-generated introspection exists in the repository, so each name is derived from Hasura's documented rules: [naming] https://hasura.io/docs/2.0/schema/postgres/naming-convention/ (Supported naming conventions; Behavior of custom table name; Backward compatibility), [query] https://hasura.io/docs/2.0/api-reference/graphql-api/query/ (By PK syntax; Aggregate object; OrderByExp), [mutation] https://hasura.io/docs/2.0/api-reference/graphql-api/mutation/ (insert (upsert) syntax; insert_one syntax; update_by_pk syntax; delete_by_pk syntax; on_conflict argument for Postgres; pk_columns argument; Mutation response). Each entry's 'cite' names the sections it rests on.",
